---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — Obsidixz Commercial"
  description="An emerging, research-led business within the Obsidixz parent brand — structured supplier research operated remotely from Nigeria for international clients."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About Us</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>An emerging research desk, run with care.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width:64ch;">
        Obsidixz Commercial is a new business doing one thing deliberately well:
        structured, sourced research that helps buyers make better-informed supplier
        decisions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <div class="wrap lede-row">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who we are</p>
        <h2 id="story-heading">Small, remote, and deliberately narrow.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Obsidixz Commercial is a business expression of the Obsidixz parent brand. It is
          not a separate legal entity and holds no claim beyond being the parent brand’s
          commercial research practice — the same family of businesses, focused here on
          procurement intelligence.
        </p>
        <p>
          The business is operated remotely from Nigeria and serves clients internationally,
          working in English. There is no showroom, no warehouse and no supplier network —
          there is a research desk, a written method and a commitment to saying what the
          evidence supports.
        </p>
        <p>
          Responsible individual and founder: <strong>Richard Oluwadunmininu Olasehinde</strong>.
          Obsidixz is an unregistered business brand; it does not claim incorporation, a
          registered office or a telephone presence it does not have.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--grey" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <h2 id="approach-heading">Principles we don’t trade away</h2>
      <div class="table-like" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
        <div><b>Sources over assertions</b><span>Every finding traces to a public source with a research date. If we cannot show where it came from, we do not present it as fact.</span></div>
        <div><b>Gaps stated, not hidden</b><span>Missing or conflicting information is marked as such. A marked gap is useful; a confident guess is dangerous.</span></div>
        <div><b>Scope before fee</b><span>Written scope and a fixed, individually tailored quotation precede any research. No surprises, no open-ended hourly work.</span></div>
        <div><b>Honest limits</b><span>If a brief is outside what we can serve — or what we can honestly verify — we say so before taking it on.</span></div>
        <div><b>Evidence over opinion</b><span>Every finding traces to a public source with a research date, and gaps are marked rather than filled in. The comparison reflects what the sources show — not a preference for any supplier or outcome.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="not-heading">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">What we are not</p>
      <h2 id="not-heading">Clear boundaries, on purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Obsidixz Commercial is a research service. It is not a marketplace or supplier
        directory, not a packaging manufacturer or converter, not a freight, shipping or
        logistics company, and not an inspection, testing or quality-assurance provider.
        It is not a procurement outsourcer and holds no purchasing authority on your
        behalf, and it does not offer escrow or payment protection.
      </p>
      <p>
        Supplier Discovery reports are built from public commercial information — they are
        a better-informed starting point for your own decisions, to be paired with your
        own verification before contracts, payments or production are approved.
      </p>
      <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.75rem; margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact">Discuss your research needs</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/services">Explore the service</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
